      "Text": "trafficserver security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for trafficserver is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Apache Traffic Server is an OpenSource HTTP / HTTPS / HTTP/2 / QUIC reverse, forward and transparent proxy and cache.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nImproper Access Control vulnerability in Apache Traffic Server.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Traffic Server: from 9.0.0 through 9.2.14, from 10.0.0 through 10.1.3.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.2.15 or 10.1.4, which fixes the issue.\n\n\n\nThis CVE supersedes CVE-2026-41920, whose record listed the affected 9.x versions as 9.0.0 through 9.1.14 and the fixed version as 9.1.15. All 9.2.x releases before 9.2.15 are affected.(CVE-2026-102795)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for trafficserver is now available for master/openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4/openEuler-24.03-LTS-Next/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3/openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of critical. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Critical",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "trafficserver",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
